   "AnchorBarGrid"], Cell["Reserved and Earlier APIs", "GuideTitle"],
  Cell[
   "Recognize historical names and use the maintained calculation workflow.",
   "GuideAbstract"], Cell["Some names remain exported for compatibility with \
old notebooks but have no callable implementation on this branch. Their \
individual pages identify that status explicitly. A help page for a reserved \
name does not make the old algorithm available.", "GuideAbstract"],
  Cell["Use ConstructAmplitude and the exact identity tools for current \
constructive work. Machine-learning simplification and evolutionary \
amplitude-search development are not required by these tools.",
   "GuideAbstract"], Cell["Current Alternatives",
   "GuideFunctionsSubsection"],
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["ConstructAmplitude", BaseStyle -> "Link",
      ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/ref/ConstructAmplitude"], ": ", "Construct\
, complete, simplify and validate an amplitude from its process and two \
models."}], "GuideText"],
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["PrepareAmplitudes", BaseStyle -> "Link",
      ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/ref/PrepareAmplitudes"], ": ", "Simplify \
diagram pairs or factorization rows while retaining their physical \
assumptions."}], "GuideText"],
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["SpinorIdentityCandidates", BaseStyle -> "Link",
      ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/ref/SpinorIdentityCandidates"], ": ", "Enu\
merates legal symbolic identity edits for a diagram or amplitude expression."}\
], "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["ApplySpinorIdentity",
      BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData ->
       "paclet:HEPCAT/ref/ApplySpinorIdentity"], ": ", "Applies a currently \
legal identity edit and returns the new expression."}], "GuideText"],
  Cell["Reserved Names", "GuideFunctionsSubsection"],
